## `spec` fields

These are the top-level fields of the Connection spec, the same as `spec:` in YAML. Nested objects are described in the
server's JSON Schema at `GET /v1/schemas` (also used by the UI builder for validation).

| Field | Type | | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `integration` | string | **required** |  |
| `description` | string | optional |  |
| `config` | map | optional | Non-secret settings. |
| `secrets` | map | optional | Connection field -> secret name. |
| `credentials` | one of `shared`, `per_user`, `per_user_or_shared` | optional | Whose credential calls use: the connection's (`shared`), the person the run acts for (`per_user`; the step waits until they connect), or theirs when they have one (`per_user_or_shared`). Default: `shared`. |
| `user_fields` | list of string | optional | Connection fields each person supplies (default: the fields in `secrets`). |
| `oauth` | object | optional | Lets people connect with OAuth instead of pasting a token. |

